Right now I'm having a great nh3.0.7 game. A very lucky start: at Dlvl 2
and Xplvl 2, I came across a cane shop. I didn't have much money or ways
to rob the shop, so I left it. Some time later, I started hearing mumbled
curses. In the room next to the shop, I came across a kobold shaman. I
kicked him to death, and it appeared he had taken two wands out of the
shop. I tried out the first one (by engraving), and it was create monster.
The kobold shaman needed only one kick, and left a piece of armor behind.
I tried out the second wand, it said: You may wish for an object ..
I wished for green dragon scale mail. Then the wand was empty. So after a
great number of tries I could have my named weapon. Finally I had time to
look at what the other kobold shaman had left behind: *gauntlets of
power*!
Without a blindfold and several other items, I haven't ventured below
level 20 yet. Some things occurred that gave the idea for improvements:

1. (trivial one) When you pick up from a spot where several kinds of items
lie, you should get *everything* when you answer "a", not all things of
the first kind.

2. I'd like to get a more elaborate message after tinning: I often drop
the tin immediately afterwards, so knowing its inventory letter would be
handy.
	You now have (q) 17 tins of green mold meat

3. *** SPOILER, MAYBE ***
I had a fight with a Golden Naga Hatchling. After I killed it, a chameleon
corpse was left behind (so that's what it actually was, I suppose).
I hadn't thought about the obvious consequences, so I ate the corpse.
After a few moves, I merged with my armor and thus became a green dragon.
(Two questions I still have are:
(1) Do you always polymorph *just once* after eating a chameleon corpse?
	(It didn't happen again the next 30.000 turns)
(2) Do you always polymorph into a green dragon when you're wearing green
dragon scale mail?)
When I returned to human form, I was very sorry, because I expected to
have lost my armor. *I hadn't!* This is a mistake in nh: my armour had
merged with me, so it shouldn't suddenly be there again when I change!
That's all.

